<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roman conquest of Britain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">43–84 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Roman conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> began with the invasion ordered by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> in 43 CE and continued in stages over the next four decades. Southern Britain was occupied quickly, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> faced resistance from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caratacus">Caratacus</a> and the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boudica">Boudica</a> in 60–61 before subduing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gnaeus-julius-agricola">Agricola</a>'s victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> Graupius in 83 or 84 marked the furthest advance into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, and Britain remained a Roman province until about 410.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roman-conquest-of-britain.jpg" alt="Roman conquest of Britain" width="320" height="598" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: my work · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman.Britain.campaigns.43.to.84.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
